00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.960
Ok, let's get stuck into some secrets and
fun facts about The Boss Baby movie!

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.410
To make sure they captured the right facial
expressions for Boss Baby, the movie's animators

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:50.160
spent many hours online watching videos of
babies, especially ones that caught a baby's

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.489
first reaction to something, for example,
a new flavour of food or seeing a pet for

00:00:54.489 --> 00:00:55.610
the first time.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:00.620
Likewise, when it came to creating the world's
cutest dog, the Forever Puppy, the animators

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.580
found their inspiration by watching tons of
online videos of super-cute puppies.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.760
And one of the movie's animators, Dan Wagner,
also brought in his rescue puppies for a visit

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.630
to the studio to further inspire his fellow
animators.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.509
During their work on early versions of the
movie, the filmmakers planned to have Boss

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:21.960
Baby's special mission team of Staci, Jimbo,
and the Triplets voiced by adult actors.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.360
However, it soon occurred to them it'd be
much funnier if they cast child actors instead

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.610
so they could play up the fact that although
the team is supposed to be there to help Boss

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.360
Baby, they actually often hinder and annoy
him, because they sometimes act and sound

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.369
more like babies than grown-ups.

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:41.260
Instead of aiming for a photo-realistic look
that's now possible in animation thanks to

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:46.560
advances in technology, The Boss Baby director
Tom McGrath wanted his movie to have a graphic,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.909
stylised aesthetic and for his characters
to be 'flexible and fleshy'.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:54.509
So, he drew inspiration from the handmade
look of the golden age of animation which

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:56.490
he and many of his crew grew up with.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.310
For example, the movie's elastic visual style
owes a lot to classic Looney Tunes and Merrie

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:05.909
Melodies cartoons and the work of legendary
animators and directors such as Tex Avery,

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:10.910
Chuck Jones, Friz Freleng, and Bob Clampett,
who brought to life stacks of iconic characters

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.590
including Bugs Bunny, Daffy Duck, Porky Pig,
Sylvester the Cat, and Road Runner.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:19.820
Indeed, Alec Baldwin, who voices Boss Baby,
says he learned a lot about playing tough,

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.050
demanding characters by watching Looney Tunes
cartoons as a child, particularly the way

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.930
voice actor Mel Blanc played characters like
Foghorn Leghorn with such swagger and authority.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.110
Various Disney animated features also influenced
the Boss Baby team, especially the charming

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:38.520
nostalgia of the 1950s classic Lady And The
Tramp, and the beautiful creations of artist

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:44.250
Mary Blair, who worked on films such as Peter
Pan, Alice in Wonderland, and Cinderella.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.490
Although The Boss Baby movie was inspired
by Marla Frazee's best-selling picture book,

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:53.090
it also draws heavily on the personal experiences
of the filmmakers and artists, who often swapped

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.220
stories with each other about their own families
during the production.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.580
For example, Tim's stuffed toy, Lamb Lamb,
was based on a much-loved toy lamb that belonged

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.910
to the daughter of the movie's screenwriter,
Michael McCullers.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.190
And it was director Tom McGrath who added
an older brother and the idea of sibling rivalry

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.280
to the movie's story as it reminded him of
his own childhood where he was the younger

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.450
brother or Boss Baby in his family.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:18.580
So, for McGrath, the film became 'a loving
homage' to his older brother.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:23.540
Originally, Miles Bakshi, who plays Tim, was
hired just to record a temporary voice track

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.260
while the filmmakers were working on their
various storyboard ideas, but they thought

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:31.620
his performance was so good that they decided
to cast him in the final movie.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.200
Like his character Tim, Miles has a younger
sibling of his own; in fact, his sister Nina

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.940
is the voice of adult Tim's daughter in the
movie!

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.060
Indeed, you could say that animation runs
in Miles's family because his grandfather

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.980
is director Ralph Bakshi, whose work includes
the adult animated feature Fritz the Cat and

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:53.280
the 1978 animated Lord of the Rings movie,
as well as the Mighty Mouse cartoon TV series

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.280
from the 1980s.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.730
And, in fact, it was Ralph Bakshi who gave
Boss Baby director Tom McGrath his first break

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.040
back in the early 90s on the movie Cool World.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.440
Jimmy Kimmel may be best known for hosting
his late-night TV talk show, but it was actually

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:10.560
hearing him being interviewed on the radio
that gave director Tom McGrath the idea of

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.520
casting the well-known TV host as Tim's dad
in the movie.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.390
And Tom McGrath actually has his own cameo
in the movie too as the voice of the TV chef

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:23.190
on the cooking show that babysitter Eugene
watches at Tim's house.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.750
By the way, if you've watched the Madagascar
movies, you'll have heard McGrath before as

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.100
the voice of the penguin leader, Skipper.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.520
And the movie also keeps things in the DreamWorks
family by casting Trolls director Walt Dohrn

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.150
as the voice of the photographer who takes
pictures of Tim and Boss Baby in their little

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.380
sailor outfits.

